    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d825">

                <pb facs="0953" n="809" xml:id="pg809"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.512/960</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >MacMurray</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Consul General at
                        Tientsin</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Gauss</hi>)<anchor n="57"
                        xml:id="d825-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-04-26">April 26, 1929</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I beg leave to acknowledge the receipt of
                    your despatch of April 22, 1929,<anchor n="58" xml:id="d825-f2"/> in which you
                    inform the Legation that by a notification issued March 20th, the Revenue Stamps
                    Tax Bureau at Tientsin, operating through the Customs Bank, has imposed certain
                    stamp taxes on goods imported from Shanghai under “Exemption Certificates,” and
                    that you have received a protest from the American Chamber of Commerce in regard
                    to such imposition. You request instructions with regard to the action to be
                    taken concerning these new stamp taxes.</p>
                <p>The Legation is of the opinion that, in the absence of some discriminatory
                    feature, either in the imposition of such taxes or their collection, the
                    Consulate General should take no action in the matter, at least for the time
                    being. In the event that there appear to be any discriminatory features in the
                    taxes, you are authorized to protest their imposition on such grounds.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">J. V. A.
                    MacMurray</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d825-f1" n="57" type="source" xml:id="d825-f1-content">
                <p>Copy transmitted to the Department by the Minister in his despatch No. 2058,
                    April 26; received June 10, 1929.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d825-f2" n="58" xml:id="d825-f2-content">
